{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985657-mystery-cults-of-the-caucuses","id":985657,"title":"Mystery Cults of the Caucuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T14:01:12-07:00","id":985657,"title":"Mystery Cults of the Caucuses","content":"This is an attempt at making a placeholder for brainstorming or presenting homebrewed Mystery Cults that are either products of the Orders or at least connected to them in some way. <br /> <br /> Personally, I love the dimension they give to the caucuses local to a setting. I'll share mine once they're fully polished. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see what some of you have been using for your Chronicles, or have simply thought up. Just sharing concept ideas is cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:36:24-07:00","id":985681,"title":"","content":"Do you mean sleeper mystery cults attached to Caucuses or the mystery cults around which caucuses gather? I'm guessing the former, although from the title I assumed the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:49:13-07:00","id":985693,"title":"","content":"Michael&gt; Sorry for the lack of clarity. I meant the former, but really either would be welcome .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:24:20-07:00","id":986087,"title":"","content":"My game is set in Dublin. Guardian's Labyrinth hasn't come up so it's not been used or fleshed out, but the Cultor poses as a leader of a group of New Age mystics who treat Irish folklore, like fairy rings and banshees, as if real, and sucker in the gullible. With a bit of the classic tarot card reading and seances with the dead to add that necessary hoodoo flair. Though the mythology itself has <i>juuust </i>enough Supernal Truth behind it she can spot people asking the right questions. Cultor in question is an Acanthus so she can easily get whatever information she needs to pull off a ruse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:20:13-07:00","id":986176,"title":"","content":"I'm currently designing a cult lead by a Proximi family pertaining to the remaining Silver Ladder caucus of Philadelphia. (Since the Seers took advantage of the former Hierarch's corruption, Libertine 'usurpers' have taken advantage of their swollen ranks to run a 'Democracy' already strained by favoritism and the challenge of keeping Mages not keen on the Assembly from getting violent) Some of its higher ups are Sleepwalkers who've proven themselves. Their praxis is to reclaim the dispossessed by setting up rehabilitation centers like halfway houses and women's shelters in some of the worst neighborhoods of Philadelphia, south and central New Jersey. Their they teach how to sever destructive patterns in their life to 'unshackle' themselves and realize their 'potential' and tap into the field of endless possibilities. The Wise who influence the Cult select those who seem more likely to Awaken and attempt to rid them of any bad spirits that might be fettered to them, influence their dreams to help them realize larger Truths, and rid them of any psychosis through the help of mind magic. Those who don't quite Awaken at least are much more empowered, and encouraged to embed themselves in influential spheres to help better the community as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:41:49-07:00","id":986188,"title":"","content":"One of my first characters set up a fraternity. Basically, it promoted itself as a frat for those who really wanted to improve their understanding of themselves and the world. They were focused on scholastic achievement as well as the charities such organizations are normally noted for; since their creed was essentially aggressive self-improvement, members pushed each other to excel at everything. They were tiny and didn't host many parties, but those that they did became legend.<br /> <br /> Whole thing was an incubator for proto-awakened souls and run by a coalition of Free Council and Silver Ladder mages. Mostly, it was a cover for their cabal, but they were also trying to draw in various sorts of souls who were pushing their Sleeping limits and to help filter out the monsters. (Ironically, one of the members <i>was</i> a monster who still honestly treated the members of the fraternity as friends. It was the <i>un</i>worthy he preyed on...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:34:19-07:00","id":986649,"title":"","content":"Okay, wordy and unpolished, but this is something I kinda wanted to run with in a game for a while.<br /> <br /> <b>Vox Populii</b><br /> <br /> This is a faction inside the Free Council of Assemblies. Its ranks include far more than just these, but that's the vast majority of its proponents. <br /> <br /> Its history varies with historian. <br /> One version claims a heritage going back to Atlantis. They claim that a group of Atlantean sages learned the truth about magic and the ways of magic and tried to direct them to listen to a higher will than one arrogant magus or a feuding group of them: The entire people. Another claims that they are as old as Athens, for fairly obvious reasons, and that the Atlantean story was a fable that the Athenean magi adopted. They both claim that they existed as an order outside Pentacle for millennia. Most consider that fable.<br /> <br /> The majority seem to believe that they are a resurgence of focused democratic principles. &quot;Democracy seeks the truth&quot; While some claim that they *are* the Free Council, most believe that the synthesis and free exchange the order promised delivered. They learned from each other and became far stronger than their hierarchical competitors ever could have imagined.<br /> <br /> <br /> To outsiders, they represent the Free Council, good and bad. To those inside the FCA, well, they simply seem a bit extreme on their interpretations of the Tenets.<br /> <br /> The group always works to establish democratic government. They seek to include Sleepers and sinister magi alike, though. They argue that Hierarchies Foster the Lie.<br /> <br /> When the Sleepers outnumber the mages sufficiently, and are spooked by magic, the Vox to clamp down on casting, or so many fear. The group really is extremely radical. They aid whoever the people truly want. If a majority vote for a candidate, that candidate has the support of the Vox Populi until they lose that support. If the office retains the support, however, they are not free to act as they wish against an unpopular candidate. Where the Vox are least initiated, they tend to have all the flaws of democracy, such as votes on votes and scrabbling to make things fit. Once some of them start to learn how to listen to the Will of the People, though, their entire process becomes streamlined.<br /> <br /> <br /> Members learn to use the Will of the People as a powerful mystical force. Their inner circle have hacked the Silver Ladder's modus operandi and figured out how their calls to supernal symbolic authority works. Members gain benefits when working as a team in ways that other magi cannot. They do lose some of their initiative, but become fantastic team players.<br /> <br /> A vote can be formal or not. The Vox must accept whatever form the vote takes.<br /> <br /> The definition of People is critical to the magic, here, and provides a fluid concept. It must, however, be a reasonably fair definition to count, hierarchy notwithstanding. A mob in its own neighborhood can easily count as a quorum of those affected. For a Vox to consider the whole city, they'd need some sort of vote from them. Persuasion is permitted, but not in a way that inhibits.<br /> A quorum of the People has the right to vote on any topic and it is <u>binding</u>. <br /> Scope limits things, practically, which is why it's so useful to hear the voice more clearly. Initiation allows this.<br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Cult Initiation:<br /> 1.</b> Gain a specialty in Persuasion(Demagoguery) representing a deep knowledge of how democracy works.<br /> <b>2.</b> The Vox begins to lose the faulty divisions of self in favor of the Cause. The Vox changes their Vice to &quot;Destroy Hierarchy&quot; meaning any meaningful attack against any system that is not a true democracy. Their Virtue becomes &quot;Promote the Will of the People&quot;. They become increasingly intuitive as to the what the will of the People is, sometimes learning about their will without needing to witness specific votes. These visions always count as if a vote was had of the highest order and works as the Mystery Commands merit.<br /> <b>3.</b> When acting in service of the Will of the People, the Vox can use that fact to empower the spell with a Yantra that adds a bonus equal to their initiation rating.<br /> <b>4.</b> The Vox adds their Initiation rating to their Willpower point pool and regain a mana when refreshing willpower through Virtue or Vice.. When acting in the the express Will of the People, the benefit of spending willpower improves to their initiation rating. This applies to efforts made to set up a vote, even where one would be impractical or attacked, or to intuit the current will.<br /> <b>5.</b> A Vox's alignment with Democracy is so strong, that they can use Democracy to literally punch through the Lie. A Supernal Verge opens in the Demesne to a realm known as The Forum. Use of Soul Stones of those attuned to Followers of the Lie, of course, ruins the effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b><br /> Those with this level of initiation are direct servants of the People, and any personal matters come second to them. They must gain an arcane beat in service of the People before they can earn one for their own petty obsessions. Most grow obsessed with mysteries that fulfil their mission, anyway, and don't feel such distractions, anymore.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:03:32-07:00","id":987426,"title":"","content":"Well I have a Mystery Cult I've been working on that is definitely tied to the Orders, but as rivals or antagonists. First a disclaimer though: this idea is heavily borrowed from an idea a friend of mine used for their D&amp;D game. Loved it so much I adopteded it for Mage. Not sure how much he borrowed from other sources himself, but the idea is super cool and hope you guys like it.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Venatori<br /> &gt; Description: Originating within the Guardians of the Veil but growing to encompass all of the Pentacle Orders and some Seers, this Banisher Nameless Order believes the Atlantean Paradigm is not only a falsehood but also one of the major sources for the Abyss. In their paradigm, the Supernal and Abyss are two sides of the same coin, and that one cannot exist without the other. So in truth the magic of the Wise comes from outside of reality from the Abyss, and will continue to grow until the &quot;Absolute Truths&quot; it spreads have been erased or forgotten by the mortals of the true reality (the Empirical World as you will.) This belief stems from the original Guardian Cabal's observations revolving around the Sleeping Curse, and the theory that it's not caused by the Exarchs at all but instead is reality's way of both protecting itself and healing the damage done from foreign influences.<br /> &gt; Purpose: Destroy not only the emanations of the Hidden Realms but also erase all knowledge and evidence of their incursion into the Empirical World.<br /> &gt; Relic: Name of Oblivion (Grimoire)<br /> &gt; Doctrine: Long ago an ancient Cabal of mages opened a hole in reality at the bequest of the Burning Ones. This allowed the magic of the Hidden Realms to infect the Empirical World, and the Cabal to harness it's power to bend the world to their will. As they drew upon this magic the hole grew into a yawning Abyss, and the world was twisted by the powers the Mages wrought. It was then that the Venatori stepped forward, a wise mortal who saw through the Burning One's poisonous whispers, and convinced half of the Cabal to turn against the others. Thus the Oblivion War began, and has been waged across the world ever since by the apprentices of the First Cabal. Only when all traces of the Hidden Realms have been removed from the Empirical World can the Abyss be healed. Only when magic has been completely forgotten can it plague mankind no longer.<br /> &gt; Perks<br /> (1) Cryptology Specialization for Academics.<br /> (2) One Dot Safe Place Merit or One Dot Alternate Identity Merit.<br /> (3) Rote Skills (Academics, Stealth, Subterfuge)<br /> (4) Three Dot Occultation Merit.<br /> (5) Four Dot Unique Paradox Eater Familiar. (Can negate one success on a Paradox Roll, but at the cost of putting the Mage into a fuge state for the remainder of the scene and directly under the ST's control)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Forgot to explain a key part of their origins. 10-14-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}